# Commits that only moved whitespace. `git blame` skips them and reports the commit that
# last changed the line's meaning, which is the one you actually want when you are asking
# why a safeguard is written the way it is.
#
# Not automatic in a fresh clone -- enable it once, per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only pure-mechanical commits belong here. A commit that changes behavior must never be
# added, or blame will quietly point past the change that matters.

